 "rule": "At each order-book snapshot of a bucket with a two-sided tradeable book, take the newest scored decision of the same city-day at or before the snapshot (at most an hour before, as test 2). If the probability p is at least THETA above the best bid, rest a bid for one YES share AT the best bid; if the best ask is at least THETA above p, rest an offer of one YES share at the best ask (the same as a bid for one NO at 1 - the ask). An order lives until the next snapshot of the bucket or an hour, whichever comes first. It is FILLED only if a trade in that bucket after the snapshot and before the order ends printed THROUGH its price: a taker selling YES (or buying NO) at a YES price below the bid, a taker buying YES (or selling NO) above the offer. A print through the price clears every order resting at it, so this does not depend on where the order would have stood in the queue. A print AT the price (the \"touch\") is shown beside it as the optimistic case, not the test. Prints come from data/archive/trades, NO-token prints turned into YES prices (1 - p). One share per bucket, side and day: the first fill. Settled on the venue's winner: a YES bought at b pays (won) - b, a YES sold at a pays a - (won). No fee (makers pay none); the maker's rebate (a quarter of the taker's fee, cost_model.maker_rebate) is shown beside, not counted. THETA 0.05 is the test; 0.02 and 0.10 beside it. The market's own normalised prices (q) and the tempered market are the controls. The window: the event dates whose books are in the repository and whose trades all carry their token (from the first archived trade file with every token known), through the newest date the mirror holds books for.",
 "test_theta": 0.05,
